  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Defense Threat Reduction (DOD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An APHIS SME was sent to Tanzania to participate in a table top exercise on zoonotic emergency disease response preparedness. The exercise used rift valley fever virus as the test disease event. The Tanzania Department of Health, Department of Agriculture, wildlife authority, and military representatives are expected to participate. Representatives from the U.S. DOD, CDC, and USDA attended. There were break out groups during the exercise for animal health SMEs and epidemiology SMEs. The USDA SME was expected to observe the exercise and provide feedback on coordination between the Tanzania government ministries from a one-health approach</narrative>
  </description>
